  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/e9ede3d8d40b90fcf4919b85917c2fa21bf91163d136a1cd40b8bd6c0db3b40d.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. Point $K$ is **not** collinear with the points $M$ and $N$\n\nII. Points $L,O,Q$ are collinear\n\nIII. Points $J,K,Q$ are **not** collinear",
  "worked_solution": "- Statement I is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/fa3ac1e9323a72254ecfc2242b1de23c05f0cc639b593eeadacb64ed6b4d4036.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/8895800b4c1ca6d22d42fac0cdb1488f716bdb5b59b49496d2f908f0947314b0.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/f39a0462a8a52762c7525e31746e69269ab4b9521f4cc4e8121b114e98ddb68a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
